e for the incident window, but already assigned to two active incidents from the database queue.\n- Ben: Confirmed available for the full 18:00 to 22:00 window.\n- Carmen: Confirmed available for the full 18:00 to 22:00 window.\n- Deepa: Confirmed available for the full 18:00 to 22:00 window and can serve as backup.\n- Eli: Available, but only serves incident manager coordination shifts.\n- Farah: Available starting at 20:00 only.\n- Gabe: Available for the full 18:00 to 22:00 window, but needs access confirmation before assignment.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":11,"totalLines":11,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/incident_staffing_plan/availability_notes.md","time":{"start":1781475932502,"end":1781475932506}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_069c11dc9214cbaa016a2f2a5c90e481918a3ebe909d285b2e"}},"id":"prt_ec83d7944001ehMCqdmRc9iiGF","sessionID":"ses_137c2d28affeWriXJ56NuiDR1y","messageID":"msg_ec83d63d1001L6Fz8oAooC1u1F"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781475932529,"sessionID":"ses_137c2d28affeWriXJ56NuiDR1y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_xFCDLAj3mjQC439RqGglKxSZ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/incident_staffing_plan/coverage_rules.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/incident_staffing_plan/coverage_rules.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Coverage Rules\n2: \n3: Incident ID: INC-4472\n4: \n5: Incident window: 2026-05-06 18:00 to 2026-05-06 22:00\n6: \n7: System: customer billing database\n8: \n9: Choose one primary responder and one backup responder.\n10: \n11: General rules:\n12: \n13: - Use local files only.\n14: - If access status appears in more than one dated source, use the newest dated source.\n15: - A responder must be available for the full incident window.\n16: - A responder must have active `db-prod` access as of the newest access source.\n17: - A responder is ineligible if they already have 2 or more active incidents.\n18: - Primary and backup must be different people.\n19: \n20: Primary rules:\n21: \n22: - Primary must have role `Database Engineer` or `SRE`.\n23: - Primary must be scheduled for `database` on-call coverage during the full incident window.\n24: \n25: Backup rules:\n26: \n27: - Backup must have role `Database Engineer` or `SRE`.\n28: - Backup does not need to be database on-call, but must be available for the full incident window and have active `db-prod` access.\n29: - If more than one backup is eligible, choose the candidate with the fewest active incidents. If still tied, choose the alphabetically first name.\n\n(End of file - total 29 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Coverage Rules\n\nIncident ID: INC-4472\n\nIncident window: 2026-05-06 18:00 to 2026-05-06 22:00\n\nSystem: customer billing database\n\nChoose one primary responder and one backup responder.\n\nGeneral rules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- If access status appears in more than one dated source, use the newest dated source.\n- A responder must be available for the full incident window.\n- A responder must have active `db-prod` access as of the newest access source.\n- A responder is ineligible if they already have 2 or more active incidents.\n- Primary and backup must be different people.\n\nPrimary rules:","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/incident_staffing_plan/coverage_rules.md","text":"# Coverage Rules\n\nIncident ID: INC-4472\n\nIncident window: 2026-05-06 18:00 to 2026-05-06 22:00\n\nSystem: customer billing database\n\nChoose one primary responder and one backup responder.\n\nGeneral rules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- If access status appears in more than one dated source, use the newest dated source.\n- A responder must be available for the full incident window.\n- A responder must have active `db-prod` access as of the newest access source.\n- A responder is ineligible if they already have 2 or more active incidents.\n- Primary and backup must be different people.\n\nPrimary rules:\n\n- Primary must have role `Database Engineer` or `SRE`.\n- Primary must be scheduled for `database` on-call coverage during the full incident window.\n\nBackup rules:\n\n- Backup must have role `Database Engineer` or `SRE`.\n- Backup does not need to be database on-call, but must be available for the full incident window and have active `db-prod` access.\n- If more than one backup is eligible, choose the candidate with the fewest active incidents. If still tied, choose the alphabetically first name.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":29,"totalLines":29,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/incident_staffing_plan/coverage_rules.md","time":{"start":1781475932518,"end":1781475932527}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_069c11dc9214cbaa016a2f2a5c90ec819182d36a325fe9c3af"}},"id":"prt_ec83d7957001yjQRevECDXlvXG","sessionID":"ses_137c2d28affeWriXJ56NuiDR1y","me